Recommends: xfce4-terminal | xterm
Suggests: network-manager-gnome, xfce4-session
Description: left-edge dock with one workspace per app
 Cubby is a dock for X11 desktops that puts every application on its own
 workspace. Opening an app moves it to a fresh workspace and adds a button to
 the dock; clicking the button jumps to that app.
 .
 It has an app drawer, pinned apps and folders, support for launchers that
 run in a terminal, a network indicator, a clock with calendar and a user
 menu. Each app can opt out of having its own workspace.
 .
 Cubby needs an X11 session with an EWMH-compliant window manager. It is
 developed on Xfce and does not work on Wayland.
